<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <Import Project="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)Local.props" Condition="Exists('$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)Local.props')" />

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net6.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>disable</ImplicitUsings>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <NoWarn>CS8632;CS8765</NoWarn>
    <RootNamespace>Stellar.CombatMeter</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Stellar.CombatMeter</AssemblyName>
    <!-- 2.7.0: rDPS P2 — the `sheet` track (the local player's damage-relevant attributes, spec § 6.1) on
         top of P1's event spool + buff track. Requires framework 2.7.0 (Abstractions 2.7.0); released
         lock-step with it. MUST NOT stay 2.6.0: the owner's MAIN client already runs a P1 build stamped
         2.6.0 and header.pluginVer is what tells the two apart server-side.
         2.7.1: testing-channel-only "upload target" setting (owner 2026-09-06) — a build stamped with
         StellarChannel=testing (below) exposes a settings toggle pointing this install's uploads at the
         dev/testing server; a plain build (StellarChannel unset → "stable") renders nothing for it.
         2.7.3: (a) a TESTING build now DEFAULTS its upload target to the testing server the first time
         it runs (until the user explicitly chooses otherwise via the settings toggle — owner "yes"
         2026-09-06); production rejects every 2.7.x upload outright, so an un-redirected testing build
         was silently uploading nothing. (b) the upload header's encounter window is clamped to a
         non-negative duration (LogUpload/CombatLogAssembler.cs's ClampEncounterWindow) — a
         `durMs=0` archive whose EnteredAtMs landed after its own ArchivedAtMs produced a NEGATIVE
         header.encounter.durationMs that the server rejected outright, failing the whole upload.
         2.8.0: rDPS phase 2 capture — (a) every player's casts as skill/101 rows off AttrSkillId
         (attr 100), (b) the sheet track grows 26→33 attrs (cooldown, versatility, haste, mastery,
         resource), (c) a buff keyframe (kf rows) opens every spool segment. Still testing channel
         only; requires framework 2.7.0 (no new framework API). Uploads only fully consumed by logs
         worker rdpsVersion ≥ 3. The archive decision now gates on real game events
         (SpoolSegment.HasGameEvents), never on cast or keyframe rows (final review C1).
         2.9.0: rDPS phase 2b (D10) — the local player's per-skill cooldown ratio is captured off the
         existing ~10 Hz LocalCooldowns snapshot (CdRatioTracker) and spooled as a DERIVED sheet row
         under the synthetic attribute id 9011960 (sheet track 33→34 attrs); every segment keyframe
         restates the last known ratio so the worker's step function has a value at segment start.
         It is a CAPTURE row: never gated by pause or a toggle, and it never counts toward
         SpoolSegment.HasGameEvents, so it can never decide an archive. No new poll, no framework
         change. The ratio is SCENE-SCOPED: cooldown buffs are DeleteChangeScene, so the tracker is
         reset on the scene change that clears the live buff set, and the next scene's keyframe
         restates nothing until a real cooldown row states the new truth.
         Consumed by logs worker rdpsVersion ≥ 5 (own-baseline bound test, D11).
         2.9.1: STABLE BUILDS ALWAYS UPLOAD TO PRODUCTION (owner 2026-09-09: "make sure combatmeter
         will point to production logs site"). Player-language note for the release: "Fixed: a leftover
         testing-server setting from the testing channel could make a stable build upload to the testing
         site; stable builds now always upload to the production logs site." Mechanism: the 2.7.3
         testing default (and the settings toggle) PERSIST the dev base into the "uploadApiBase" pref,
         so any install that ever ran a 2.7.3+ testing build carried it forever — and a stable build
         renders no Upload-target toggle to undo it with, so it kept uploading to dev with no way out.
         A stable build now CLEARS a configured base equal to the testing one (normalised compare:
         whitespace / case / trailing-slash tolerant) and logs that it did, UNGATED. Any other non-empty
         base (the owner-only staging override) is still honoured untouched; the testing-channel path is
         unchanged (testers keep their dev target). Decision stays the pure
         Plugin.ResolveInitialUploadTarget. -->
    <!-- 2.10.0: Appearance → Bars → "Bar colour: Role | Class" (owner 2026-09-09: "combat meter should
         have an option on appearance to be able to toggle to show role gauge color or class gauge
         color"). Per layout (list / party5 / party20) under "{prefix}.bar.color"; DEFAULT Role, so no
         existing install's meter changes until the user opts in. Class paints the player gauges (main
         bar, the spine when it is in DPS mode, history chart series, archived history rows, skill
         breakdown bars) with ClassPalette — the game's own class crest colours, byte-identical to the
         logs site's classColor(). Unknown class → the role colour. The HP spine is untouched.
         Rollback-safe: a ≤ 2.9.1 build never reads "bar.color" and is unaffected by its presence. No
         upload, archive, stage or run-identity behaviour is touched — colour only.
         Appearance → Bars → "Value text: Plain | Outline | Shadow" (owner 2026-09-09: "it should be
         option for players 1. normal text, outline, smooth shadow") — controls how the per-second/total
         values drawn ON a row's bar stay readable over the fill, via the new MeterRowData.LabelStyle
         (framework 2.8.0, Stellar.Abstractions.Services.MeterLabelStyle). Per layout under
         "{prefix}.bar.labelStyle"; DEFAULT Plain (today's white text), so no existing install's meter
         changes until the user opts in, and a ≤ 2.10.0-pre build never reads "bar.labelStyle" and is
         unaffected by its presence. Requires framework 2.8.0 (Abstractions 2.8.0) — see the
         PackageReference note below for the local-feed situation; the version there must be flipped to
         2.8.0 once the framework release publishes, and the registry manifest's minimum framework
         becomes 2.8.0 at that point too. -->
    <!-- 2.11.0: upload resilience (PR #46, branch fix/upload-resilience — the base of this stack). The
         header re-send retry, the per-track send guards, and the bounded wait on a segment's blob writes.
         That work never bumped this property (the owner's MAIN client runs a build stamped via
         `-p:Version=2.11.0`), so the number is recorded here and the value jumps 2.10.0 -> 2.12.0.
         2.12.0: EVENT CHUNKS UPLOAD BROTLI-COMPRESSED (owner 2026-09-22: "why gzip when we already use
         brotli?"). Player-language changelog bullet for the release:
           * "Uploads are far smaller and much faster — a chunk of combat data now goes out about 27x
              smaller, so a long raid finishes uploading in seconds instead of minutes."
         Mechanism: LogUpload/ChunkCompressor.cs + the HTTP send in LogUpload/ChunkUploader.cs POST the
         envelope as `Content-Encoding: br` (brotli quality 9, window 22, one-shot System.IO.Compression
         BrotliEncoder — BCL only, no new dependency). The logs api accepts and STORES the client's bytes
         as received (StellarLogs main d85d194c, live on api.stellarresonance.app and on dev); chunks were
         already stored brotli at rest, so this removes the server's re-compression instead of adding one.
         Nothing in capture / archive / spool / run identity / the buff send filter is touched: the same
         bytes go to the same endpoints in the same order — only the transfer encoding changes.
         An upload is NEVER lost to compression: an unavailable encoder (the native compression library
         failing under BepInEx's .NET 6 runtime on Wine) and a server answering 415 both fall back to the
         byte-identical plain JSON the 2.11.0 path sent, each logging ONE line per process; the 415 resend
         is immediate and does not consume one of the chunk's retries. Requires no framework change and no
         minModSystemVersion bump. -->
    <!-- 2.13.0: CombatMeter joins the Stellar plugins window (owner feature request, Toir 2026-09-17:
         CombatMeter was "in a limbo of being a plugin and not being in the plugin window"). It was the
         only tool plugin that registered NO launcher entry, so its history + settings were reachable only
         through the meter overlay's header menu — a player who hid the meter had to unhide it just to open
         history or link an account. Two launcher tiles now expose CombatMeter's config WITHOUT the meter
         being visible (Plugin.Launcher.cs): a ⚙ "CombatMeter" tile opens the uploads/auto-archive Settings
         window, and a 🕘 "Combat History" tile opens the history window; both are shown only in the World
         phase (like Wardrobe / LoadoutSwitcher). Account → "Link to site" moved from its own standalone
         window into a section at the bottom of the Settings window (it is upload-related) and its meter
         header button was removed. Player-language changelog bullet:
           * "CombatMeter is now in the Stellar plugins window — open your combat history or settings
              straight from there, without turning the meter on first. 'Link to site' moved into settings."
         No capture / archive / stage / run-identity / upload behaviour is touched — this is UI wiring
         only. Requires no framework change and no minModSystemVersion bump. -->
    <!-- 2.14.0: PARTY-MODE PLAYER DEBUFF ICONS (owner request 2026-09-24; spec
         docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-party-debuff-icons-design.md). The party-focus rows (5-player
         column + raid-20 grid) now show each member's active debuffs as a fixed-width 2×2 icon block on
         the far right — icon + ×N stacks badge + a radial duration sweep (like the game's party frame),
         up to 4 with a "+N" overflow. Because the block is a constant width, every DPS bar now ends at
         the same x (fixes the uneven-bar look). Player-language changelog bullet:
           * "Party mode now shows each member's debuffs as icons on the right of their row — with stacks
              and a countdown, like the game's party frame."
         Data source: the combat wire (ICombatLookup.BuffsFor) for every member, filtered to real debuffs
         (BuffInfo.IsDebuff + a display icon, minus a tunable denylist), ordered stable-FIFO, remaining
         time from ServerNowMs. New per-mode Appearance toggle "Show debuffs" (default on, party tabs only).
         Display only — NO capture/archive/stage/run-identity/upload behaviour is touched. Requires the
         framework build that adds MeterRowData.Debuff0..3/DebuffOverflow/ShowDebuffs + DebuffSlot + the
         2×2 renderer (Abstractions >= 2.10.0; referenced here as 2.10.0-dev until the framework releases). -->
    <Version>2.14.0</Version>
    <Deterministic>true</Deterministic>
    <AppendTargetFrameworkToOutputPath>false</AppendTargetFrameworkToOutputPath>
    <!-- Build-time release-channel stamp (registry CI sets -p:StellarChannel=testing for its testing-
         channel target). Unset (plain `dotnet build` — CI's default lane, local builds) = "stable".
         Read at runtime via AssemblyMetadataAttribute (Plugin.UploadTarget.cs); gates a settings-only
         UI surface, never upload/capture behaviour itself. -->
    <StellarChannel Condition="'$(StellarChannel)' == ''">stable</StellarChannel>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <AssemblyMetadata Include="StellarChannel" Value="$(StellarChannel)" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Requires framework 2.7.0: CombatEvent.BuffChanged.FirerId/SourceKind/SourceId (rDPS capture,
         spec 2026-09-05). 2.7.0 is NOT yet published: this repo's
         committed NuGet.config <clear/>s sources down to nuget.org only, so local builds actually
         resolve 2.7.0 from the global NuGet package cache (~/.nuget/packages/stellar.abstractions/
         2.7.0), seeded there by an earlier `dotnet restore -s nuget.org -s .localfeed` against the
         devkit's local pack (dotnet pack of Stellar.Abstractions) — NOT from a committed local-feed
         source. Purge that cached unpublished 2.7.0 before any post-publish verification build, or
         a stale local pack will silently shadow the real published package. Plugin CI stays red
         until the framework 2.7.0 release publishes. The registry manifest's minModSystemVersion
         must be raised to match at release.
         2.8.0-dev bump (2.10.0 feature, "Value text" appearance option): requires framework 2.8.0's
         MeterRowData.LabelStyle, also NOT yet published — resolved here against the devkit's local pack
         at .localfeed/Stellar.Abstractions.2.8.0-dev.nupkg (restore with both the local feed AND
         nuget.org as sources, since the committed NuGet.config sources nuget.org only). MUST be flipped
         from "2.8.0-dev" to plain "2.8.0" once the framework 2.8.0 release publishes; the registry
         manifest's minimum framework must be raised to 2.8.0 at that same release.
         2.10.0-dev bump (party-focus debuff icons, spec 2026-09-24-party-debuff-icons-design.md): requires
         framework 2.10.0's MeterRowData.Debuff0..3/DebuffOverflow/ShowDebuffs + the DebuffSlot struct, also
         NOT yet published — resolved against the devkit's local pack at
         .localfeed/Stellar.Abstractions.2.10.0-dev.nupkg (same local-feed + nuget.org restore-source
         situation as the 2.8.0-dev bump above). MUST be flipped from "2.10.0-dev" to plain "2.10.0" once the
         framework 2.10.0 release publishes; the registry manifest's minimum framework must be raised to
         2.10.0 at that same release. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Stellar.Abstractions" Version="2.10.0-dev" />
    <PackageReference Include="Stellar.PluginContracts" Version="2.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Stellar.Plugin.InteropRefs" Version="2.0.0" />
    <!-- Managed ECDSA. System.Security.Cryptography's ECDsa is OS/CNG-backed and its SignData throws
         NTE_NOT_SUPPORTED (0x80090029) under Wine/Proton, breaking signed uploads + per-install claims
         (P2-SIGNING, 2026-06-30). BouncyCastle is pure-managed — works identically on Windows AND Wine.
         Merged into the single plugin DLL by ILRepack.targets on Release (the deploy copies only that
         one DLL; the framework loads plugins via Assembly.LoadFile with no sibling-dependency probing). -->
    <PackageReference Include="BouncyCastle.Cryptography" Version="2.5.0" />
    <!-- Build-only: merges BouncyCastle into Stellar.CombatMeter.dll on Release (see ILRepack.targets).
         PrivateAssets=all so it never flows to the test project's transitive build. -->
    <PackageReference Include="ILRepack.Lib.MSBuild.Task" Version="2.0.34.2" PrivateAssets="all" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Resources/mic.png" LogicalName="Stellar.CombatMeter.mic.png" />
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Resources/headphone.png" LogicalName="Stellar.CombatMeter.headphone.png" />
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Resources/mute.png" LogicalName="Stellar.CombatMeter.mute.png" />
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Resources/settings-gear.png" LogicalName="Stellar.CombatMeter.settings-gear.png" />
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Resources/history.png" LogicalName="Stellar.CombatMeter.history.png" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- i18n catalogs: auto-discovered by the framework via the Lang.<code>.json suffix (framework 2.1.0). -->
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Lang/en.json" LogicalName="Stellar.CombatMeter.Lang.en.json" />
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Lang/ja.json" LogicalName="Stellar.CombatMeter.Lang.ja.json" />
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Lang/th.json" LogicalName="Stellar.CombatMeter.Lang.th.json" />
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Lang/id.json" LogicalName="Stellar.CombatMeter.Lang.id.json" />
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Lang/fil.json" LogicalName="Stellar.CombatMeter.Lang.fil.json" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Remove="tests/**/*.cs" />
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Stellar.CombatMeter.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
